 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "A seal for the covenant, coins for the small price; stars on «السماوات» leave before the Name, then geometric. 189 is not glossed. STAGING v4: 187-188: those given the Book (dark robes) hold it (read) beside the people they were to explain it to, then turn their backs on «فنبذوه وراء ظهورهم» (Al-Muyassar: فتركوا العهد); the covenant is a seal plate, the small price a coins plate (no one is drawn paying them, since the tafsirs do not name who paid). 188: they speak, pleased with what they did (As-Sa'di: زعموا أنهم هم المحقون في حالهم ومقالهم); the punishment is not pictured. 189 stays ambient: Allah's dominion and power."
 },
